  "inversion": {
    "data_types": [
      "regional_waveforms"
    ],
    "method": "Nonnegative least-squares finite-fault inversion of regional broadband waveforms (13 stations), with Laplacian smoothing, damping and moment minimization; rupture velocity 2.5 km/s and rise time 0.2 s. Digitized from the published Fig. 9 slip color map.",
    "green_function_model": "Regional broadband synthetic Green's functions; time-domain moment-tensor calculations use frequency-wavenumber integration with the Novotny et al. (2001) velocity model.",
    "slip_type": "variable",
    "smoothing_constraint": true,
    "notes": "FIGURE-DIGITIZED, NOT ORIGINAL INVERSION PATCH VALUES. Figure 9 (Jan 27 Mw5.3) shows color scale 0-40 cm and axes -6 to +6 km along strike (North to South) and -5 to +5 km along dip. This file samples approximate color at centers of a 12 x 10 grid (1 x 1 km); it does not claim this was the inversion mesh. Along-strike distance is measured from the figure's northern edge; down-dip grid index is assigned from the top of the printed figure, but the geographic dip direction is not resolved. Depths are inferred from a planar dip of 84 degrees and 14-km hypocenter at the plotted origin and are not independently published patch depths. Patch geocoordinates are unavailable. Patch rake is held at the preferred nodal-plane value -154 degrees from Table 1; patch-specific rake is not reported. The reported ~5 x 4 km concentrated slip region, 40-cm peak, 13-cm mean and 20-km2 rupture area are paper estimates, not grid-wide statistical summaries. The zero-valued figure background is retained in the sampled mesh. The segment reference_point is set approximately at the earthquake epicenter for geobrowser display, not a surveyed upper-edge endpoint."
  },
